import Basis from '../../layouts/Basis.astro';
---
<Basis
  titel="Privacy policy | Slim Geregeld Administratie"
  omschrijving="How Slim Geregeld Administratie handles your personal data: what, why, for how long, who it is shared with, cookies and your rights."
  taal="en"
  cta="/daft/contact/"
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap lees">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="datum">Last updated: 21 November 2026. The <a href="/privacybeleid">Dutch version</a> is leading.</p>

      <h2>1. Who I am</h2>
      <p>Slim Geregeld Administratie, sole proprietorship of Kyle Bouwmeester.<br>
      Slijpakker 14, 1541 TE Koog aan de Zaan, the Netherlands<br>
      KVK 92596991 · VAT NL004963420B24<br>
      <a href="mailto:kyle@slim-geregeld.nl">kyle@slim-geregeld.nl</a></p>

      <h2>2. What data I process</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, email address and phone number</li>
        <li>Business name, KVK number and VAT number</li>
        <li>Administrative data, such as invoices, receipts, bank transactions and annual figures</li>
        <li>Data for your tax return or permit documents, when I prepare them</li>
        <li>Messages by WhatsApp and email</li>
        <li>What you fill in on a form on this website</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide my services: your bookkeeping, returns, permit documents and Slim (performance of the contract)</li>
        <li>To meet legal obligations, such as the tax retention period and anti money laundering rules (Wwft)</li>
        <li>To stay in touch and answer your questions</li>
        <li>To improve this website, only with your consent (see cookies)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How long I keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Administrative data: 7 years (Dutch tax retention period)</li>
        <li>Client communication: 3 years</li>
        <li>A form without becoming a client: at most 1 year</li>
        <li>Other data: as long as you are a client, plus at most 1 year</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Who I share it with</h2>
      <p>I never sell data. I only share it with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The Dutch Tax Administration, the IND and other authorities, when the law requires it or when you ask me to</li>
        <li>Suppliers I need for my work, under a data processing agreement or their standard processor terms, such as Moneybird (bookkeeping), Google Workspace (email and storage), Meta (WhatsApp Business), OpenAI (reading receipts and messages in Slim, not used to train models), Netlify (this website and its forms) and my own automation server hosted in Amsterdam</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>On your first visit I ask whether you accept cookies. Without consent I only use what the site needs to work, and I count visits without cookies and without knowing who you are.</p>
      <p>With your consent I use Google Analytics (via Google Tag Manager) to see how the site is used, and Dealfront, which shows from which company a visit comes based on the IP address. It does not identify people.</p>
      <p>You can change your choice at any time via <a href="#" onclick="window.sgCookieInstellingen&&sgCookieInstellingen();return false">Cookie settings</a>, also at the bottom of every page.</p>

      <h2>7. Security</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Encrypted connections (SSL)</li>
        <li>Strong passwords and two-step verification where possible</li>
        <li>Professional software and secure storage</li>
        <li>Regular backups</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access, correct, delete (as far as the law allows), object to and transfer your data. Email <a href="mailto:kyle@slim-geregeld.nl">kyle@slim-geregeld.nl</a> and I will handle it within a month.</p>

      <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
      <p>Not happy with how I handle your data? Let me know first. You can also file a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority, the <a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Basis>

